---
import Monument from './Monument.astro';
import { site } from '../consts';
---

<div class="intro">
  <Monument backdrop />

  <div class="column intro__body">
    <div class="title-row">
      <span class="title-row__mark">
        <img src="/mark.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
      </span>
      <h1>{site.fullName}</h1>
    </div>

    <p class="intro__lead">
      <a href={site.axiomsSsccs}>SSCCS</a> is a geometric computing model: a computation is an{' '}
      <a href={`${site.whitepaperHtml}#observation-and-projection`}>observation</a> over a coordinate
      space, not a sequence of instructions. That space is composed of immutable{' '}
      <a href={`${site.whitepaperHtml}#definition-of-primitives`}>{'Segments, a Scheme, and the dynamic Fields'}</a>{' '}
      that bound the admissible set. Parallelism and verifiability follow from that structure rather
      than from added mechanisms, and near-linear scalability and energy efficiency follow with them.
      State is the result of projection, and time is one coordinate among many.
    </p>
    
    <p class="intro__sub"></p>
    
    <p>
      The <a href={site.axioms}>{site.organization}</a> develops the model, guided by its{' '}
      <a href={site.direction}>operational direction</a> and <a href={site.philosophy}>philosophy</a>.
      It reaches current silicon through open stacks that run the full pipeline, from formal
      specifications through the software toolchain, a compiler and a runtime, to the open hardware
      architecture. Those stacks rest on three shared layers:{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/projects/syntagma">synTagma</a>,{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/projects/nexus">neXus</a>, and{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.ssccs.org/projects/kinetics">kineTics</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="intro__open">
      <a href="#brief" data-depth-open>The brief</a>
    </p>
    
    
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* The scene is held behind the opening block and bleeds past it on every side,
     so the model is present before the reader reaches the Model section. */
  .intro {
    position: relative;
  }

  .intro__body {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  /* The title carries the mark and the name on one centred line. The mark is
     clipped by its round frame, so the corners of the square drawing are cut by
     the circle rather than floating inside it. */
  .title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 4cap;
  }

  .title-row__mark {
    display: block;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .title-row__mark img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  /* The opening statement, then one line at a lower rank that says what the stack
     is made of. A rule divides the statement from the detail that follows. */
  .intro__lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .intro__sub {
    color: var(--fg-3);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }

  /* The control that opens the brief below, an outlined box on the page colour,
     runs the same open and scroll as the group's own header. */
  .intro__open {
    margin: 28px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .intro__open a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 8px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: none;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .intro__open a:hover {
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .title-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .title-row h1 {
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
